(1477622, 191582, 31005, '<td valign="top">nice angle.</td>', 'nice angle.', '2005-06-23 06:26:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1477633, 193989, 31443, '<td valign="top">Your idea is a real good one and the focus if fine, but I''m guessing you are new to DPC and for a small image you will be voted down :(  you are allowed to post images up to 640 pixels any which way and it sure makes a lot of difference in quality.</td>', 'Your idea is a real good one and the focus if fine, but I''m guessing you are new to DPC and for a small image you will be voted down :(  you are allowed to post images up to 640 pixels any which way and it sure makes a lot of difference in quality.', '2005-06-23 06:38:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(1477634, 193950, 35229, '<td valign="top">Wow!!! Love it! Makes me wanna shift.</td>', 'Wow!!! Love it! Makes me wanna shift.', '2005-06-23 06:38:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1477635, 192212, 31443, '<td valign="top">I like the image sharpness and quality but imo cropping could have been better and more effective using horizontal and showing more of the handle..</td>', 'I like the image sharpness and quality but imo cropping could have been better and more effective using horizontal and showing more of the handle..', '2005-06-23 06:40:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1477636, 194036, 37380, '<td valign="top">This is a great photo, but appears to be let down by the fact that you are saving the image with too much compression. This has introduced artefacts around some of the edges.  If you''re interested, there''s an article in the tutorial section on how to use Photoshop to prepare images and it covers saving jpeg files to make the most of the 150k limit available to us. Even though you might not be using Photoshop, similar actions are available in other (some even free) image editing applications.<br/> <br/>But now for some comments on the photo:<br/> <br/>I think that you have picked a very interesting subject, which many people may never have seen before. This should do well in this challenge. The lighting of the subject is very good - with no obvious bright or distracting hightlights. The background colour compliments your subject well. Despite the jpeg artifacts I mentioned earlier, I think that this image still holds up extremely well against the rest of the competition. <br/> <br/>Good luck!</td>', 'This is a great photo, but appears to be let down by the fact that you are saving the image with too much compression. This has introduced artefacts around some of the edges.  If you''re interested, there''s an article in the tutorial section on how to use Photoshop to prepare images and it covers saving jpeg files to make the most of the 150k limit available to us. Even though you might not be using Photoshop, similar actions are available in other (some even free) image editing applications. But now for some comments on the photo: I think that you have picked a very interesting subject, which many people may never have seen before. This should do well in this challenge. The lighting of the subject is very good - with no obvious bright or distracting hightlights. The background colour compliments your subject well. Despite the jpeg artifacts I mentioned earlier, I think that this image still holds up extremely well against the rest of the competition.  Good luck!', '2005-06-23 06:40:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(1477637, 193990, 31443, '<td valign="top">Pity about the background...</td>', 'Pity about the background...', '2005-06-23 06:43:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1477638, 191430, 37380, '<td valign="top">The background is distracting, but the watch is perfectly in focus. Unlike many other entries in this challenge, the I feel that ''reflection'' aspect adds to the overall image. Both the watch and the reflection are well lit. The bronze/copper colours have really been captured well.</td>', 'The background is distracting, but the watch is perfectly in focus. Unlike many other entries in this challenge, the I feel that ''reflection'' aspect adds to the overall image. Both the watch and the reflection are well lit. The bronze/copper colours have really been captured well.', '2005-06-23 06:44:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1477639, 193070, 31443, '<td valign="top">Could have been much nicer with a better focus, idea is good..</td>', 'Could have been much nicer with a better focus, idea is good..', '2005-06-23 06:45:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1477641, 192686, 28801, '<td valign="top">Needs better illumination</td>', 'Needs better illumination', '2005-06-23 06:52:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1477642, 193159, 37380, '<td valign="top">A great photo. Personally (just my opinion, take with a grain of salt), I would have cropped out all of the balcony above, even though it would mean lopping off part of the larger pipes. This would have given a more uniform background to the rest of the pipes.<br/> <br/>The focus is great but what I''m really amazed by are the absolutely gorgeous colours in the pipes - especially the blues at the bottom. That definitely gives it the ''wow'' factor in my book.<br/> <br/>Overall, a very nice and original entry - well done!</td>', 'A great photo. Personally (just my opinion, take with a grain of salt), I would have cropped out all of the balcony above, even though it would mean lopping off part of the larger pipes. This would have given a more uniform background to the rest of the pipes. The focus is great but what I''m really amazed by are the absolutely gorgeous colours in the pipes - especially the blues at the bottom. That definitely gives it the ''wow'' factor in my book. Overall, a very nice and original entry - well done!', '2005-06-23 06:55:40.000000', NULL, 1),
