(1490882, 192870, 22734, '<td valign="top">Arpita: A truly awe inspiring image and three blues to speak highly of your outstanding efforts. Well, you have a new ardent fan here and I look forward to your future entries.<br/> <br/>Congratulations on your BLUE!</td>', 'Arpita: A truly awe inspiring image and three blues to speak highly of your outstanding efforts. Well, you have a new ardent fan here and I look forward to your future entries. Congratulations on your BLUE!', '2005-06-29 11:03:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(1490888, 194087, 36050, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by sabphoto:</b></div><hr/><i>Very cool (pun intended) image.  Did you freeze the ball then let it melt some?  Great idea, nice lighting and color tones.  Even like the overexposed white spot on the front, helps show its metal. <br/> <br/>Good luck </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yes, I made a big block of ice with the ball inside. Then I used water to melt it.<br/> <br/>Thanks for the comment, I like very much how you describe the score you''re giving.</td>', 'Originally posted by sabphoto:Very cool (pun intended) image.  Did you freeze the ball then let it melt some?  Great idea, nice lighting and color tones.  Even like the overexposed white spot on the front, helps show its metal.  Good luck   Yes, I made a big block of ice with the ball inside. Then I used water to melt it. Thanks for the comment, I like very much how you describe the score you''re giving.', '2005-06-29 11:04:18.000000', NULL, 0),
