(1491348, 194083, 33899, '<td valign="top">thanks for the comments everyone! they''ve all been very helpful :)</td>', 'thanks for the comments everyone! they''ve all been very helpful :)', '2005-06-29 12:48:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(1491384, 193492, 19936, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments.  I agree about the distractions in the lower right and left.  Cropping them out just looked worse to me and being a basic challenge I had to leave them in.  As for over shapening I seem to be having a problem with that on images with quite a bit of detail.  As I did not add any sharpening to this photo throughout the process I think it might be in my rezizing.  Still working on it.  Overall I''m pretty happy with this score. <br/> <br/>Thanks again to all who voted and commented.</td>', 'Thanks for all the comments.  I agree about the distractions in the lower right and left.  Cropping them out just looked worse to me and being a basic challenge I had to leave them in.  As for over shapening I seem to be having a problem with that on images with quite a bit of detail.  As I did not add any sharpening to this photo throughout the process I think it might be in my rezizing.  Still working on it.  Overall I''m pretty happy with this score.  Thanks again to all who voted and commented.', '2005-06-29 12:55:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(1491404, 191019, 19936, '<td valign="top">Great job Chuck!  Although I did not comment I did like this image.  Pretty cool (and weird) looking building.</td>', 'Great job Chuck!  Although I did not comment I did like this image.  Pretty cool (and weird) looking building.', '2005-06-29 12:58:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(1491436, 194072, 31213, '<td valign="top">CONGRADULATIONS on your first top 10 finish! Wooohooooo!!! :))))</td>', 'CONGRADULATIONS on your first top 10 finish! Wooohooooo!!! :))))', '2005-06-29 13:05:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(1491445, 192870, 37893, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your blue. I knew this would win from the start! Great composition and overall eye for a subject that has been photographed a million times before.</td>', 'Congratulations on your blue. I knew this would win from the start! Great composition and overall eye for a subject that has been photographed a million times before.', '2005-06-29 13:06:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(1491474, 192870, 28742, '<td valign="top">WOW! Excellent shot! Beautiful and unique for that bridge, I think. You have an incredible way of making ordinary things look extraordinary! Congratulations!</td>', 'WOW! Excellent shot! Beautiful and unique for that bridge, I think. You have an incredible way of making ordinary things look extraordinary! Congratulations!', '2005-06-29 13:12:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(1491535, 191582, 28742, '<td valign="top">I shoulda known it was you, Frank. Great finish with an excellent shot! Congrats!</td>', 'I shoulda known it was you, Frank. Great finish with an excellent shot! Congrats!', '2005-06-29 13:26:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(1491578, 192870, 3724, '<td valign="top">Wonderful image, colour is perfectly realized.  Warm and a sense of mystery at the same time!</td>', 'Wonderful image, colour is perfectly realized.  Warm and a sense of mystery at the same time!', '2005-06-29 13:36:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(1491624, 194078, 18552, '<td valign="top">This is so pretty, Harvey.</td>', 'This is so pretty, Harvey.', '2005-06-29 13:48:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(1491644, 192870, 38400, '<td valign="top">Amazing ! I like the way the bridge seems to lead to, well...notin :)<br/>Great picture</td>', 'Amazing ! I like the way the bridge seems to lead to, well...notin :)Great picture', '2005-06-29 13:54:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(1491658, 193989, 30222, '<td valign="top">its cute")</td>', 'its cute")', '2005-06-29 14:01:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(1491679, 192817, 38238, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments on my pic.  I am new to this site and didn''t realize my picture could have been larger.  My Bad!  I just wanted to add that this picture was taken at Disneyland at night with not tripod use.  I did not modify or touch the pic. in any way shape or form.  What I shot is what you see.  It also seems that in the voting most people don''t look for that in a photo.  So it would seem that this is more of a photoshop contest and not photography.  Interesting.</td>', 'Thanks for the comments on my pic.  I am new to this site and didn''t realize my picture could have been larger.  My Bad!  I just wanted to add that this picture was taken at Disneyland at night with not tripod use.  I did not modify or touch the pic. in any way shape or form.  What I shot is what you see.  It also seems that in the voting most people don''t look for that in a photo.  So it would seem that this is more of a photoshop contest and not photography.  Interesting.', '2005-06-29 14:09:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(1491728, 194000, 22379, '<td valign="top">Scuds - i gave you a 6. From the second i read the metal challenge, i wished i had some mercury to play with, so naturally i was happy to see someone with a mercury pic. <br/>The strongest aspect of the image is the splash of the mecury as it hits the bowl, and the twist in the poured line. I was not a fan of the large blob of prepoured mecury (probably from previous attempts, right).<br/>For me, the image would have ben stronger (8-9) if you had let go of the soup in a bowl concept and gotten closer to the action. ALthough understandable you wouldn''t want the mecury on your camera - a zom perhaps rather than macro. <br/>The lighting was a little iffy for me also, i would have prefered the bowl to be soild white rather than a gradient shading to the back of the bowl, for a higher score. <br/>I really love the tiny droplets that had rolled away from the main attraction, i think it might have been interesting to be down on thier level rather than up above. I can tell you enjoyed taking this picture - and thats what matters most of all ;) <br/></td>', 'Scuds - i gave you a 6. From the second i read the metal challenge, i wished i had some mercury to play with, so naturally i was happy to see someone with a mercury pic. The strongest aspect of the image is the splash of the mecury as it hits the bowl, and the twist in the poured line. I was not a fan of the large blob of prepoured mecury (probably from previous attempts, right).For me, the image would have ben stronger (8-9) if you had let go of the soup in a bowl concept and gotten closer to the action. ALthough understandable you wouldn''t want the mecury on your camera - a zom perhaps rather than macro. The lighting was a little iffy for me also, i would have prefered the bowl to be soild white rather than a gradient shading to the back of the bowl, for a higher score. I really love the tiny droplets that had rolled away from the main attraction, i think it might have been interesting to be down on thier level rather than up above. I can tell you enjoyed taking this picture - and thats what matters most of all ;) ', '2005-06-29 14:27:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(1491746, 193032, 22379, '<td valign="top">Gave you an 8 Papa. This picture coupled with the title made me chuckle. Always a good start. Great concept, great composition, clever use of the theme, appropriate dop coupled with an interseting scene. I am not sure how i feel about the sepia. I think i would have liked the touch of green from the trees. Could have used a tiny bit more tinkering with curves to tone down some of the white spots. One of my favourites in this challenge.</td>', 'Gave you an 8 Papa. This picture coupled with the title made me chuckle. Always a good start. Great concept, great composition, clever use of the theme, appropriate dop coupled with an interseting scene. I am not sure how i feel about the sepia. I think i would have liked the touch of green from the trees. Could have used a tiny bit more tinkering with curves to tone down some of the white spots. One of my favourites in this challenge.', '2005-06-29 14:30:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(1491769, 194058, 36353, '<td valign="top">Thought I''d reciprocate since you were nice enough to give me a comment.<br/> <br/>I liked this one. It made me laugh because my wife does stamping and scrapbooking, so glitter everywhere is part of my life. I thought, "Oh man, she''s gonna have a mess to clean up!" Glad you had fun shooting it.<br/> <br/>I like the blurry glitter in the air, as it makes for a nice captured action shot. The lips were in the perfect place and deliver their message immediately. The crop was perfect as well.</td>', 'Thought I''d reciprocate since you were nice enough to give me a comment. I liked this one. It made me laugh because my wife does stamping and scrapbooking, so glitter everywhere is part of my life. I thought, "Oh man, she''s gonna have a mess to clean up!" Glad you had fun shooting it. I like the blurry glitter in the air, as it makes for a nice captured action shot. The lips were in the perfect place and deliver their message immediately. The crop was perfect as well.', '2005-06-29 14:37:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(1491784, 192698, 22379, '<td valign="top">I gave a 6. And i completely disagree with charmed - your choice of an interesting angle was the reason i gave you a 6. This isnt a stock photography site, its an artistic venture; bring on these original perspectives i say. I also like that you were up close and personal with the pop, for the same reason. Its nice to see a macro that isnt a flower/bug/water droplet. <br/>The focus seems to be on the blue patten on the can, i would have prefered it to be on the 2 lines that become the drinking hole thing (i dont drink soda, i dont know what its called haha). <br/>I''m not entierly sure the image *is* noisey, or if it is just the texture of the metal and the pixelated pattern that pop cans are printed with?<br/></td>', 'I gave a 6. And i completely disagree with charmed - your choice of an interesting angle was the reason i gave you a 6. This isnt a stock photography site, its an artistic venture; bring on these original perspectives i say. I also like that you were up close and personal with the pop, for the same reason. Its nice to see a macro that isnt a flower/bug/water droplet. The focus seems to be on the blue patten on the can, i would have prefered it to be on the 2 lines that become the drinking hole thing (i dont drink soda, i dont know what its called haha). I''m not entierly sure the image *is* noisey, or if it is just the texture of the metal and the pixelated pattern that pop cans are printed with?', '2005-06-29 14:40:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(1491803, 190998, 22379, '<td valign="top">this was probably my highest scoring fishing photo in the challenge Cheryl - i gave a 6. The old pal pail really added an interest factor that the other fishing photos sadly lacked. It definatley made me think of "fishing with grandad" even though we never used such a pail or rod. <br/>Good use of b&amp;w, great lighting. <br/>I think awider  aperture might have favored this photo, just to make the reel a little sharper. I think i might have pulled everything a bit closer in on the table also, so that the pattern ran though to the top of the image, rather than thier being a empty black space. <br/>Nice image with a touch of nostalgia.</td>', 'this was probably my highest scoring fishing photo in the challenge Cheryl - i gave a 6. The old pal pail really added an interest factor that the other fishing photos sadly lacked. It definatley made me think of "fishing with grandad" even though we never used such a pail or rod. Good use of b&w, great lighting. I think awider  aperture might have favored this photo, just to make the reel a little sharper. I think i might have pulled everything a bit closer in on the table also, so that the pattern ran though to the top of the image, rather than thier being a empty black space. Nice image with a touch of nostalgia.', '2005-06-29 14:46:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(1491826, 192803, 22379, '<td valign="top">Obvious i gave this a 1, because i knew it was your photo through my super pyschic powers! No really, a 5. Techically, the picture is good. The white could have been a little brighter is my only technical critique.  The picture just didn''t speak to me. It didn''t excite my senses and blow my mind. It didn''t defrag my harddrive or do my laundry! It didn''t hit me where it hurts.<br/>I do like the twistly neck on the light source though - oh what fun you could have with that!</td>', 'Obvious i gave this a 1, because i knew it was your photo through my super pyschic powers! No really, a 5. Techically, the picture is good. The white could have been a little brighter is my only technical critique.  The picture just didn''t speak to me. It didn''t excite my senses and blow my mind. It didn''t defrag my harddrive or do my laundry! It didn''t hit me where it hurts.I do like the twistly neck on the light source though - oh what fun you could have with that!', '2005-06-29 14:51:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(1491829, 192698, 37719, '<td valign="top">I just thought with the endless possibilities for this challenge that entering a soda can was a cop out and did nothing for me when voting.  The shot is clear and the angle is interesting, the subject is boring.</td>', 'I just thought with the endless possibilities for this challenge that entering a soda can was a cop out and did nothing for me when voting.  The shot is clear and the angle is interesting, the subject is boring.', '2005-06-29 14:52:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(1491846, 193139, 22748, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the top20 placing, I think this should have been a lot higher. It''s so clean, I can''t get over it. I think this is my #1 favorite in the challenge.</td>', 'Congrats on the top20 placing, I think this should have been a lot higher. It''s so clean, I can''t get over it. I think this is my #1 favorite in the challenge.', '2005-06-29 14:55:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(1491850, 194070, 22379, '<td valign="top">I gave you a 4 shutterpug. The water is great, it has a very smooth sailing to it. I would have liked to see either the whole boat, or part of the boat coming into thew fram and the rest water where the boat will be travelling (if that makes sense). The white seems a little over exposed - it looks like there were windows but they got lost in a sun glare? As much as i dont care for nasty black smoke, the smoke is trianling nicely from your boat to the end of the screen.</td>', 'I gave you a 4 shutterpug. The water is great, it has a very smooth sailing to it. I would have liked to see either the whole boat, or part of the boat coming into thew fram and the rest water where the boat will be travelling (if that makes sense). The white seems a little over exposed - it looks like there were windows but they got lost in a sun glare? As much as i dont care for nasty black smoke, the smoke is trianling nicely from your boat to the end of the screen.', '2005-06-29 14:57:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(1491879, 190672, 22379, '<td valign="top">Buzzmom, i gave a 4. I felt that you could have gotten the model to suck a little of the spit off thier teeth before taking the picture. As other comments have stated, its a little difficult to look at and appriciate. The contrast is good, the actual braces could probably have been sharper. <br/>If this was my picture, i would have rotated it so that the braces formed a fairly straight line across the picture, rather than sloping down wards - it is amazing what a differents a coulpe of degrees of rotation can give you.</td>', 'Buzzmom, i gave a 4. I felt that you could have gotten the model to suck a little of the spit off thier teeth before taking the picture. As other comments have stated, its a little difficult to look at and appriciate. The contrast is good, the actual braces could probably have been sharper. If this was my picture, i would have rotated it so that the braces formed a fairly straight line across the picture, rather than sloping down wards - it is amazing what a differents a coulpe of degrees of rotation can give you.', '2005-06-29 15:03:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(1491909, 192435, 7743, '<td valign="top">Self Critique<br/> <br/>Overall I liked the placement of the window handle and how the focus falls off behind it.  I also liked the texture showing in the wood frame of the window.<br/> <br/>It could use more light on the handle as has been pointed out in one of the comments received so as to bring out more of the detail of the handle.  <br/> <br/>Not much wow factor due to the lack of lighting.  As it is I desaturated the colours that appeared in the background so the window frame and handle would stand out more.<br/></td>', 'Self Critique Overall I liked the placement of the window handle and how the focus falls off behind it.  I also liked the texture showing in the wood frame of the window. It could use more light on the handle as has been pointed out in one of the comments received so as to bring out more of the detail of the handle.   Not much wow factor due to the lack of lighting.  As it is I desaturated the colours that appeared in the background so the window frame and handle would stand out more.', '2005-06-29 15:10:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(1491924, 192435, 22379, '<td valign="top">I gave a 5 - i thought it was at a bus or train station but on a train! sweet! The focus and dop is really good - but it is a little hard to tell that it is good because it blends into the bar behind it. I too would have liked to see this image brighten up - maybe it would help with the above problem...</td>', 'I gave a 5 - i thought it was at a bus or train station but on a train! sweet! The focus and dop is really good - but it is a little hard to tell that it is good because it blends into the bar behind it. I too would have liked to see this image brighten up - maybe it would help with the above problem...', '2005-06-29 15:14:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(1491942, 192342, 36888, '<td valign="top">I was spooned out of third!!!!;)  Great clean photo! Congrats</td>', 'I was spooned out of third!!!!;)  Great clean photo! Congrats', '2005-06-29 15:19:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(1491960, 194058, 7743, '<td valign="top">Overall I liked your creativity with this one.  The placement of the lips etc. gives a good sense of what is happening in the image.  The soft focus in the background works really well however I found the OOF foreground a bit distracting.</td>', 'Overall I liked your creativity with this one.  The placement of the lips etc. gives a good sense of what is happening in the image.  The soft focus in the background works really well however I found the OOF foreground a bit distracting.', '2005-06-29 15:24:12.000000', NULL, 0),
