(1492086, 191429, 38267, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the top 20 finish Mike.  As I said in my comments prior to the results, I think this was one of my favorite shots and I think it was better than some of the other shots in the challenge...especially the 3rd place finisher.  Well done.</td>', 'Congrats on the top 20 finish Mike.  As I said in my comments prior to the results, I think this was one of my favorite shots and I think it was better than some of the other shots in the challenge...especially the 3rd place finisher.  Well done.', '2005-06-29 16:06:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(1492167, 191135, 22379, '<td valign="top">I gave you a 6 Alienyst - i thought you were brave for using a not rusted/ not shiney type of metal like zinc. Being an aussie, zinc to me is the white crap we smear acorss out noses on sunny days - which is what i instantly thought of seeing these bars (zinc oxide sunscreen comes in bars like chapsticks).<br/>At first i thought they were wrapped in metall paper like a crayon, afterwards realising that it was back-lit. A very affective use of this technique that definately gave the picture a little extra oomph. <br/>The image is sharp, and the light sort of draws you back though the gaps. The zinc fades a bit too much for my liking into the background in the bottom row, i would have liked to see that nice bluishblack in the top of the pile in all the rods. <br/>I wonder if this wouldnt be more interesting if it was taken from a slight angle, so that the pyramid wasn''t facting us head on, but you could still see the light down the rods. <br/>As i have said, a brave, and nicely exicuted photo.</td>', 'I gave you a 6 Alienyst - i thought you were brave for using a not rusted/ not shiney type of metal like zinc. Being an aussie, zinc to me is the white crap we smear acorss out noses on sunny days - which is what i instantly thought of seeing these bars (zinc oxide sunscreen comes in bars like chapsticks).At first i thought they were wrapped in metall paper like a crayon, afterwards realising that it was back-lit. A very affective use of this technique that definately gave the picture a little extra oomph. The image is sharp, and the light sort of draws you back though the gaps. The zinc fades a bit too much for my liking into the background in the bottom row, i would have liked to see that nice bluishblack in the top of the pile in all the rods. I wonder if this wouldnt be more interesting if it was taken from a slight angle, so that the pyramid wasn''t facting us head on, but you could still see the light down the rods. As i have said, a brave, and nicely exicuted photo.', '2005-06-29 16:30:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(1492200, 193493, 22379, '<td valign="top">My first reaction John, was "what a perfect place for a photo shoot!" meaning portraiture of course. I gave you a 6. I love the subject matter. I was born in england, and my first crush was on postman pat, so i always find an old red letter box endearing. <br/>I think the composition is interesting, i like that the image goes red/greenish/red in the three layers. I do feel that you oversharpened the image - as evident from the jaggity feel of the first 2 lamposts visable. I''m so glad these old fellas will be refurbished and not left to an infinate rust!</td>', 'My first reaction John, was "what a perfect place for a photo shoot!" meaning portraiture of course. I gave you a 6. I love the subject matter. I was born in england, and my first crush was on postman pat, so i always find an old red letter box endearing. I think the composition is interesting, i like that the image goes red/greenish/red in the three layers. I do feel that you oversharpened the image - as evident from the jaggity feel of the first 2 lamposts visable. I''m so glad these old fellas will be refurbished and not left to an infinate rust!', '2005-06-29 16:38:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(1492226, 191528, 22379, '<td valign="top">a 7 Nick. I wonder why the voters san camera hated this so much??<br/>What appealed to me most was the contrast of old and new. The rust vs the shiney metal of the lock.<br/>The red seems a touch over saturated? Did you up it, or is rust that brilliant in NZ? The compostion is good, focus great, obviously im a fan of the subject matter. I didnt care for the yellow line in the bottom left corner - i would have liked it to be soild black - but i guess not a lot you could do on that one! Not in basic anyways ;)</td>', 'a 7 Nick. I wonder why the voters san camera hated this so much??What appealed to me most was the contrast of old and new. The rust vs the shiney metal of the lock.The red seems a touch over saturated? Did you up it, or is rust that brilliant in NZ? The compostion is good, focus great, obviously im a fan of the subject matter. I didnt care for the yellow line in the bottom left corner - i would have liked it to be soild black - but i guess not a lot you could do on that one! Not in basic anyways ;)', '2005-06-29 16:45:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(1492241, 193926, 22538, '<td valign="top">Looks like the folks either loved it or hated it. There certainly is a highly personal touch visible here, and the camera is SO big:-)  Well done!</td>', 'Looks like the folks either loved it or hated it. There certainly is a highly personal touch visible here, and the camera is SO big:-)  Well done!', '2005-06-29 16:49:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(1492253, 194058, 36616, '<td valign="top">Would have given a 8 if I had had the time to vote.<br/>Mostly excellent, especially the hit you in the face obviousness. Liked the soft focus as well - it fitted with the subject nicely.<br/> Possibility of non metallic glitter is the spoiler for this challenge.<br/></td>', 'Would have given a 8 if I had had the time to vote.Mostly excellent, especially the hit you in the face obviousness. Liked the soft focus as well - it fitted with the subject nicely. Possibility of non metallic glitter is the spoiler for this challenge.', '2005-06-29 16:52:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(1492346, 193898, 22379, '<td valign="top">i honestly could not tell what it was-but it was clear to me by its shinniness and reflective nature it was metal - so i took it to be an intentional abstract, and liked it. I gave a 6. You used the three coloured lights very well imho, and i dont thinnk the "blown highlights" hurt in this case, since it obviously is a reflective object, it is an expected and forgivable, even complimentary "fault". <br/>Personally i would have roatd clockwise abit more so the white reflections in the bottom were more parallel with the border. Good to see youre using work hours to improve photography!! :D</td>', 'i honestly could not tell what it was-but it was clear to me by its shinniness and reflective nature it was metal - so i took it to be an intentional abstract, and liked it. I gave a 6. You used the three coloured lights very well imho, and i dont thinnk the "blown highlights" hurt in this case, since it obviously is a reflective object, it is an expected and forgivable, even complimentary "fault". Personally i would have roatd clockwise abit more so the white reflections in the bottom were more parallel with the border. Good to see youre using work hours to improve photography!! :D', '2005-06-29 17:09:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(1492373, 192878, 22379, '<td valign="top">oops - missed ya! <br/>I gave you a 6. I wasn''t sure if it was steam or glare that gave the hazy look above the engine - so i gave you the benifit of the doubt. It does however take from the image as a whole. I like the angle, and i think it was a good idea to desat the train. The crop is a little too tight at the top of the picture,i would have liked to see a bit more up top.</td>', 'oops - missed ya! I gave you a 6. I wasn''t sure if it was steam or glare that gave the hazy look above the engine - so i gave you the benifit of the doubt. It does however take from the image as a whole. I like the angle, and i think it was a good idea to desat the train. The crop is a little too tight at the top of the picture,i would have liked to see a bit more up top.', '2005-06-29 17:15:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(1492383, 194058, 35357, '<td valign="top">Too many entries for me to go through my usual rounds of voting &amp; sorting, so I didn''t vote, but did look through all the entries.  I would have given you an 8, but I''m a chronic high-score-giver :-P.  I remember your shot in particular out of the hundreds, which says something for sure.  I like the more human, emotive, twist.  When thrown in with so many cold photos of objects, it''s good to see a nice pair of lips.  There''s nothing I don''t like about your photo and it''s certainly strong in the creativity department, which is an important element to me.  How could it have been better?  I think it may have been even better if lighting was set up to illuminate only face, hands, &amp; glitter.</td>', 'Too many entries for me to go through my usual rounds of voting & sorting, so I didn''t vote, but did look through all the entries.  I would have given you an 8, but I''m a chronic high-score-giver :-P.  I remember your shot in particular out of the hundreds, which says something for sure.  I like the more human, emotive, twist.  When thrown in with so many cold photos of objects, it''s good to see a nice pair of lips.  There''s nothing I don''t like about your photo and it''s certainly strong in the creativity department, which is an important element to me.  How could it have been better?  I think it may have been even better if lighting was set up to illuminate only face, hands, & glitter.', '2005-06-29 17:18:08.000000', NULL, 0),
