(1492904, 194058, 37719, '<td valign="top">So we are even - 6 here too.  I liked the concept and thought it was interesting to look at.  But I kept finding myself distracted by the lips and was always drawn to them, hence ignoring the metal aspect. Perhaps if you?? weren''t wearing the red lipstick it may have helped.  Perhaps I am a sucker for red lipstick.  After looking at it some more (I view all entries at least three times) I found I kept looking for the top of the picture even though the whole image was on my screen.  Not sure why.  I thought it was I wanted to see the eyes to show the focus, but still not sure looking at it again.  But yet again I found myself trying to scroll higher to see more of the image.</td>', 'So we are even - 6 here too.  I liked the concept and thought it was interesting to look at.  But I kept finding myself distracted by the lips and was always drawn to them, hence ignoring the metal aspect. Perhaps if you?? weren''t wearing the red lipstick it may have helped.  Perhaps I am a sucker for red lipstick.  After looking at it some more (I view all entries at least three times) I found I kept looking for the top of the picture even though the whole image was on my screen.  Not sure why.  I thought it was I wanted to see the eyes to show the focus, but still not sure looking at it again.  But yet again I found myself trying to scroll higher to see more of the image.', '2005-06-29 19:30:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(1492925, 192501, 24841, '<td valign="top">WOW!  This is an amazing shot.  I have the same camera an have never made anythign look that good!</td>', 'WOW!  This is an amazing shot.  I have the same camera an have never made anythign look that good!', '2005-06-29 19:40:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(1492942, 192047, 10818, '<td valign="top">Great composition, nice focus.  Looks great in B &amp; W.  A well done macro shot.</td>', 'Great composition, nice focus.  Looks great in B & W.  A well done macro shot.', '2005-06-29 19:47:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(1492955, 193954, 37200, '<td valign="top">I liked this shot and the angle.  Maybe just a few pixels more on the left so the corner isn''t cut off...but just a few.  It seems some others didn''t care for the tilt, I wonder if you tilted it the other way so the handle was horizontal if it would have made a difference (positive or negative).</td>', 'I liked this shot and the angle.  Maybe just a few pixels more on the left so the corner isn''t cut off...but just a few.  It seems some others didn''t care for the tilt, I wonder if you tilted it the other way so the handle was horizontal if it would have made a difference (positive or negative).', '2005-06-29 19:50:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(1492963, 192870, 38267, '<td valign="top">This was actually taken from on the bridge... walking along the bridge towards Presidio, there''s a lookout point at the base of the towers. This was shot from there, leaning outwards from the bridge. I actually would have liked more of an angle, but that would need me to be suspended over the water somehow :)...<i>text</i> <br/> <br/>Thanks for the additional information.  I know exactly where you took this now.  Once again, great shot!!  Seeing as how our foggy summer season is approaching, there should be more opportunities for fog shots of the bridge in the upcoming month and a half.  Congrats!!!</td>', 'This was actually taken from on the bridge... walking along the bridge towards Presidio, there''s a lookout point at the base of the towers. This was shot from there, leaning outwards from the bridge. I actually would have liked more of an angle, but that would need me to be suspended over the water somehow :)...text  Thanks for the additional information.  I know exactly where you took this now.  Once again, great shot!!  Seeing as how our foggy summer season is approaching, there should be more opportunities for fog shots of the bridge in the upcoming month and a half.  Congrats!!!', '2005-06-29 19:54:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(1492987, 192047, 15242, '<td valign="top">I need 8 comments to get to 1000, so why not...<br/> <br/>I didn''t hit this one in voting, but would have given it a 5 or 6.  Composition and B&amp;W are great.  I can''t tell if you used too much USM or not enough, but the detail/texture just isn''t there as I''d like to see it.  Also, there is some specs or something making noise in the upper left part.  Better detail and clean up the noise and I''d give it an 8.<br/> <br/>Good job!</td>', 'I need 8 comments to get to 1000, so why not... I didn''t hit this one in voting, but would have given it a 5 or 6.  Composition and B&W are great.  I can''t tell if you used too much USM or not enough, but the detail/texture just isn''t there as I''d like to see it.  Also, there is some specs or something making noise in the upper left part.  Better detail and clean up the noise and I''d give it an 8. Good job!', '2005-06-29 20:10:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(1493023, 191319, 34591, '<td valign="top">I really want to thank everybody for all their nice comments. I''m overwhelmed by the sentiments. Thank you all again.</td>', 'I really want to thank everybody for all their nice comments. I''m overwhelmed by the sentiments. Thank you all again.', '2005-06-29 20:20:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(1493024, 194000, 32792, '<td valign="top">I''m really glad with my picture, and also it''s score! Thanks for all the votes and comments.<br/> <br/>Now to some answers:<br/>*R2 is the name of that little white robot on StarWars. Just thought it would be a funny title.<br/>*It''s kinda hard to work with mercury, because of it''s liquid form, it just won''t sit still.<br/>*As a shiny metal, it reflects the environment around it! Was I didn''t have anything large enough to reflect on the bigger "blob", I switched off the ceilling''s lights, in order to reflect only "darkness". I wish I could have wdone something to enhance it''s "metallic" appearance and form, but that was just not possible! The funny thing is, I''ve just read an article on a very popular brazilian photography magazine, which deals with lighting on reflective objects, including metal! A bit too late I think. Oh well....<br/> <br/>Here are some outtakes, and some diff ideas:<br/>no editing besides resize ---- <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=197788" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/32792/thumb/197788.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/32792/thumb/197788.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/32792/thumb/197788.jpg"/></a> ---- <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=197789" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/32792/thumb/197789.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/32792/thumb/197789.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/32792/thumb/197789.jpg"/></a> ---- <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=197790" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/32792/thumb/197790.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/32792/thumb/197790.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/32792/thumb/197790.jpg"/></a> ---- <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=197791" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/32792/thumb/197791.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/32792/thumb/197791.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/32792/thumb/197791.jpg"/></a></td>', 'I''m really glad with my picture, and also it''s score! Thanks for all the votes and comments. Now to some answers:*R2 is the name of that little white robot on StarWars. Just thought it would be a funny title.*It''s kinda hard to work with mercury, because of it''s liquid form, it just won''t sit still.*As a shiny metal, it reflects the environment around it! Was I didn''t have anything large enough to reflect on the bigger "blob", I switched off the ceilling''s lights, in order to reflect only "darkness". I wish I could have wdone something to enhance it''s "metallic" appearance and form, but that was just not possible! The funny thing is, I''ve just read an article on a very popular brazilian photography magazine, which deals with lighting on reflective objects, including metal! A bit too late I think. Oh well.... Here are some outtakes, and some diff ideas:no editing besides resize ----  ----  ----  ---- ', '2005-06-29 20:21:05.000000', NULL, 0),
