(1575884, 190676, 37893, '<td valign="top">Hey great capture here. IMO I would have darkened the upper right hand corner of the photo so that it matches with the lower left hand corner. I like the tilt of the camera here and it''s extremely very effective. Good shot!</td>', 'Hey great capture here. IMO I would have darkened the upper right hand corner of the photo so that it matches with the lower left hand corner. I like the tilt of the camera here and it''s extremely very effective. Good shot!', '2005-07-31 14:13:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(1584319, 193160, 22748, '<td valign="top">I love this image!! It''s so nice, not only should it have placed higher, it should have won first place. I like it more than the ribboners!!</td>', 'I love this image!! It''s so nice, not only should it have placed higher, it should have won first place. I like it more than the ribboners!!', '2005-08-03 15:45:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(1587222, 192904, 37779, '<td valign="top">The cropping was a little too tight, but a good idea! I really like the tones. Neatimage this with not so tight of a crop and it''d be fantastic.</td>', 'The cropping was a little too tight, but a good idea! I really like the tones. Neatimage this with not so tight of a crop and it''d be fantastic.', '2005-08-04 18:13:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(1598673, 192904, 22734, '<td valign="top">Okay: this was a good concept because of the angle. A way to improve this image is to close down aperture two more stops, this will bring the shutter speed to about 1/45. You focus on the tip. Closing another notch making the speed 1/20 would deepen the dof even more. In other words, when you shoot at this angle the dof has to capture the front and back.<br/> <br/>However, you have the idea and the vision. Just a little tweaking and the camera will respond.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-08-09 20:02:56.</i></td>', 'Okay: this was a good concept because of the angle. A way to improve this image is to close down aperture two more stops, this will bring the shutter speed to about 1/45. You focus on the tip. Closing another notch making the speed 1/20 would deepen the dof even more. In other words, when you shoot at this angle the dof has to capture the front and back. However, you have the idea and the vision. Just a little tweaking and the camera will respond.', '2005-08-09 21:01:35.000000', '2005-08-09 21:02:56.000000', 0),
(1609909, 194082, 19672, '<td valign="top">that''s pretty creative.... nice</td>', 'that''s pretty creative.... nice', '2005-08-14 16:46:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(1627745, 192468, 18932, '<td valign="top">A little strange, but an eye-catching attempt at the challenge nonetheless. The ring and fingers are not quite focussed enough for mine.</td>', 'A little strange, but an eye-catching attempt at the challenge nonetheless. The ring and fingers are not quite focussed enough for mine.', '2005-08-21 10:17:13.000000', NULL, 0),
